# The Firebase config stays out of the runtime version (fingerprint).
# CI checkouts never have the gitignored google-services.json, the EAS worker
# gets it from the GOOGLE_SERVICES_JSON file variable (written under
# ../eas-environment-secrets/), and a developer may keep a local copy. With
# the file hashed, `eas build` on CI and the build on EAS computed different
# runtime versions and EAS failed the build. The package name in it is
# already part of the app config, and a new Firebase project needs a new
# build anyway (docs/variaveis-de-ambiente.md, GOOGLE_SERVICES_JSON).
google-services.json
**/eas-environment-secrets/**
